    {
      "heading": "PULSE EHI Hyperlink",
      "style": "Heading 1",
      "paragraphs": [
        "The EHI Tables export contains the electronic health information available in a patient's Pulse record in a computable xml document format. Some electronic health information might not be available in a format, such as rich text documents or images.",
        "The content included in the export might vary based on a variety of factors, including:",
        "The software applications in use at the health system that generated the files.",
        "The documentation and software use practices in place at the health system that generated the files.",
        "Configuration decisions made by the health system that generated the files.",
        "For a standards-based way of exchanging health information, we recommend reviewing the following.",
        "This PULSE EHI information will be available https://www.chs.net/pulse-ehr-information/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Clinical Document Architecture (CDA)",
      "style": "Heading 2",
      "paragraphs": [
        "When exchanging patient summary documents, we use Clinical Document Architecture (CDA) as the content standard. CDA is an XML-based markup standard defined by Health Level Seven (HL7), intended to specify encoding, structure and semantics of clinical documents for the purpose of exchange. This document can be viewed as human readable format by using \"CDA.xsl\" stylesheet. A copy can be download it from:  https://github.com/HL7/CDA-core-xsl/blob/master/CDA.xsl",
        "Sample xml electronic readable document."
      ]
    }
  ],
